# Bresenham Circle Drawing Algorithm

## Definition

The Bresenham Circle Drawing Algorithm is an efficient raster graphics algorithm used to draw a circle using only integer calculations.

It avoids floating-point arithmetic, making it faster than traditional methods.

---

## Steps

Input:

- Center (xc, yc)
- Radius r

Initialize:

x = 0

y = r

Decision Parameter:

d = 3 - 2r

Repeat while x <= y

If d < 0

d = d + 4x + 6

Else

d = d + 4(x - y) + 10

y--

Increment x

Plot all eight symmetric points

---

## Advantages

- Integer calculations only
- Fast execution
- High accuracy
- Widely used in Computer Graphics

---

## Time Complexity

O(r)

---

## Space Complexity

O(1)
